<title>USA: U.S weekly chain store sales up 0.2 pct - Mitsubishi.</title>
<headline>U.S weekly chain store sales up 0.2 pct - Mitsubishi.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales rose 0.2 percent in the week ended August 24 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were up 5.1 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index rose 0.4 percent from the prior month.</p>
<p>&quot;Back-to-school sales appeared to be the driving factor for the week, and (school-related) sales were largely in line with retailers' sales expectations,&quot; said the report.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
